      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T16:12:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the semantics of `skipInputBytes`, again? We\u0027re adjusting `bytesToSkip` here (as if we intend to use the remainder to further adjust our position in the stream), but we don\u0027t do that anywhere. It seems like the implementation of this needs to include some kind of loop where we keep reading chunks and feeding them to the scanner, until we\u0027ve effectively seeked past the requested number of bytes? (Analogous to what happens in BufferedSourceMgr).",
      "revId": "f9859187dfd65154119c0ea8d426a57cec710c60",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
