      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T22:31:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "YES you\u0027re right! YIKES!\n\nThis should read bytesToSkip, not \"default of fBuffer-\u003esize()\". And then we need to loop to account for the fact that bytesToSkip can be \u003e fBuffer-\u003esize().\n\nI found that this path is exercised by `images/icc-v2-gbr.jpg` (it has a huge APP segment that we ignore). It crashed (when using a non-seekable stream) before this.",
